---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy & Telemetry Policy — Max">
  <div class="space-y-10 font-mono">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#162334] pb-6 space-y-2">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs text-emerald-400">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
        <span>PRIVACY & DATA SOVEREIGNTY</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white">
        Privacy, Sovereignty & Zero Tracking
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Modern web software has devolved into surveillance capitalism. This website rejects user tracking completely.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The Core Commitments -->
    <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-lg bg-[#070c14] border border-emerald-900/40 space-y-6">
      <div class="border-b border-[#141e2e] pb-3 text-xs text-emerald-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
        CORE PRIVACY INVARIANTS
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded bg-[#03060a] border border-[#141e2e] space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-white flex items-center space-x-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-400">✓</span>
            <span>Zero Third-Party Trackers</span>
          </span>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            There are no Google Analytics, Facebook Pixels, Hotjar, or advertising tracking beacons embedded in this website. Ever.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded bg-[#03060a] border border-[#141e2e] space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-white flex items-center space-x-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-400">✓</span>
            <span>Zero Tracking Cookies</span>
          </span>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            No session cookies or tracking identifiers are placed on your machine. You will never see an annoying cookie consent banner here because there is nothing to consent to.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded bg-[#03060a] border border-[#141e2e] space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-white flex items-center space-x-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-400">✓</span>
            <span>Local-First Computation</span>
          </span>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            Features like search index querying, CRT scanline toggles, guestbook entries, and Web Audio synthesis run entirely client-side in your own browser's JavaScript engine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded bg-[#03060a] border border-[#141e2e] space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-white flex items-center space-x-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-400">✓</span>
            <span>Static Generation</span>
          </span>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
            All pages are pre-compiled into static HTML, CSS, and lightweight JS via Astro 5, served statically via GitHub Pages CDN without server logging databases.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Philosophical Note -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-[#070c14] border border-[#162334] space-y-3">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider block">
        PHILOSOPHICAL STANCE
      </span>
      <blockquote class="text-xs text-emerald-400/90 italic font-mono border-l-2 border-emerald-500/50 pl-4 py-1 leading-relaxed">
        "Governments seek control. Corporations seek influence. Trust neither blindly. We rely on layers of abstractions we don't understand. It's time to build from the ground up."
      </blockquote>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed pt-2">
        Data sovereignty is not merely a legal requirement; it is a fundamental design principle. The web should be an open library of knowledge and creative experimentation, not an extraction engine.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
